  "body": "**What:** when a face-drilling cycle (G83/G84/G85) in `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` arrives with the tool not already on the hole at R, the post writes ONE combined X+Z rapid to the R point before the cycle. It does not seat the way #994's `cycleSeat` does for the mill posts, where the tool climbs to R first if it is below R, then moves over the hole, then descends. A combined X+Z rapid from below R toward the face could pass through the part or the work's face.\n\n**Today it is latent:** the axial-drill stream always arrives at R on the axis first, so the combined rapid only crosses free air (recorded as dropped in `docs/decisions/1011-lathe-cycle-exit.md`, PR #1025). A foreign/legacy stream, or a future generator that starts a cycle from a different position, would expose it.\n\n**Expected:** a face cycle that starts off-seat is seated by the hop law (Z out to at least R first, then X onto the centre, then down), or refused by name; it is never reached by one diagonal rapid below R.\n\n**Done means:** a synthetic stream that starts a face cycle from below R and off-centre posts the seated sequence (or a named refusal) on fanuc-lathe, pinned with the #1011 checker; tormach-lathe is checked (it posts no cycle); goldens that move are listed.\n\nFollows #1011 / PR #1025 (stack on it) and #994 / PR #1019.\n",
